{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 1. Quick Working Example: Fetching Public API Data\n",
"\n",
"In this initial example, we use Python's requests library to fetch JSON currency exchange rate data from a public REST API and transform it directly into a clean Pandas DataFrame."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"import requests\n",
"import pandas as pd\n",
"\n",
"# Endpoint URL for public exchange rates\n",
"url = "https://api.exchangerate-api.com/v4/latest/USD"\n",
"\n",
"# Execute GET request\n",
"response = requests.get(url)\n",
"\n",
"if response.status_code == 200:\n",
"    data = response.json()\n",
"    # Convert rates key-value pairs into a two-column DataFrame\n",
"    df = pd.DataFrame(list(data['rates'].items()), columns=['Currency', 'Rate'])\n",
"    print("Data extracted successfully!")
",
"    print(df.head(10))\n",
"else:\n",
"    print(f"Failed to retrieve data. Status Code: {response.status_code}")\n",
"\n",
"# Output assertion for verification\n",
"assert not df.empty, "DataFrame should not be empty upon successful retrieval."\n",
"assert 'Currency' in df.columns and 'Rate' in df.columns, "Columns must match expected schema.""
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 2. Parsing Nested JSON Payload with pd.json_normalize()\n",
"\n",
"Real-world financial and API responses often contain nested dictionaries and arrays. Using standard DataFrame constructors can leave complex objects unparsed. pd.json_normalize() flattens nested structures into a clean tabular layout."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"import pandas as pd\n",
"\n",
"# Sample nested JSON payload simulating a market data response\n",
"nested_api_response = [\n",
"    {\n",
"        "ticker": "AAPL",\n",
"        "exchange": {"name": "NASDAQ", "country": "US"},\n",
"        "metrics": {"price": 185.50, "pe_ratio": 28.4}\n",
"    },\n",
"    {\n",
"        "ticker": "MSFT",\n",
"        "exchange": {"name": "NASDAQ", "country": "US"},\n",
"        "metrics": {"price": 420.20, "pe_ratio": 35.1}\n",
"    }\n",
"]\n",
"\n",
"# Normalize nested structure into flat columns\n",
"df_normalized = pd.json_normalize(nested_api_response)\n",
"print(df_normalized)\n",
"\n",
"# Verify flattened column structure\n",
"expected_cols = ['ticker', 'exchange.name', 'exchange.country', 'metrics.price', 'metrics.pe_ratio']\n",
"assert list(df_normalized.columns) == expected_cols, "Columns were not correctly flattened.""
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 3. Production Error Handling & Timeout Management\n",
"\n",
"Robust production scripts must gracefully handle HTTP errors, bad gateway responses, timeouts, and unexpected data schema shifts using explicit try-except blocks."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"import requests\n",
"import pandas as pd\n",
"\n",
"def fetch_api_to_dataframe(endpoint_url):\n",
"    try:\n",
"        # Set a 10-second timeout for responsiveness\n",
"        response = requests.get(endpoint_url, timeout=10)\n",
"        response.raise_for_status()  # Raises HTTPError for 4xx/5xx codes\n",
"        payload = response.json()\n",
"        \n",
"        if 'rates' in payload:\n",
"            df_res = pd.DataFrame(list(payload['rates'].items()), columns=['Currency', 'Rate'])\n",
"            return df_res\n",
"        else:\n",
"            raise KeyError("Key 'rates' not found in JSON payload.")\n",
"            \n",
"    except requests.exceptions.HTTPError as http_err:\n",
"        print(f"HTTP error occurred: {http_err}")\n",
"    except requests.exceptions.Timeout:\n",
"        print("The request timed out.")\n",
"    except Exception as err:\n",
"        print(f"An error occurred: {err}")\n",
"    return None\n",
"\n",
"# Test function with valid API endpoint\n",
"df_validated = fetch_api_to_dataframe("https://api.exchangerate-api.com/v4/latest/USD")\n",
"print(f"Rows extracted: {len(df_validated) if df_validated is not None else 0}")\n",
"assert df_validated is not None, "Execution failed on a valid endpoint.""
]
},
